# A golden is checked by regenerating it and comparing bytes, so the bytes in
# the working tree have to be the bytes the recorded command writes. `core.
# autocrlf` is on for this checkout, and v2's table writer sets
# `lineterminator="\n"` explicitly — without this, every reproduction of
# `tests/goldens/oracle_stirred/*.csv` differs from the committed copy on every
# line, on Windows only, for a reason that has nothing to do with what was
# measured.
#
# Only the tables. The README beside them is written through `Path.write_text`,
# which does translate, so it wants exactly the default treatment and pinning it
# here would break the comparison in the other direction.
tests/goldens/**/*.csv text eol=lf
